  "notes": "Captured with WebFetch on 2026-10-13. argos.co.uk pages are client-rendered and the fetch was cut off inside the mega menu, so the homepage body, category grids, search results, product body, trolley (/basket returned a server error), sign-in form and order-tracking form could not be read; their expects use only the page titles (Track your order, Results for gta 6, Video Games & Gaming Consoles, Voucher Codes and Offers, Advice and inspiration, Login) plus well-known labels (Sign in / Email address / Password, Your trolley). Homepage items therefore use the header promo flyout and the persistent footer blocks (Returning an item, Payment methods, Follow us, Download our app) that every argos.co.uk page carries, captured verbatim from the help centre and store finder. The footer and legal bar were captured verbatim from help.argos.co.uk/help. The mega menu lists hundreds of subcategories; the sitemap section uses each department plus the first links of each menu column. argos.co.uk has no HTML site map (only sitemap.xml with 12 child sitemaps), so /sitemap is the clone's own HTML directory. web.archive.org is blocked for this host. Off-site footer links (Sainsbury's corporate, careers, privacy hub, Argos for Business, pet insurance, spares, product support) become local summary pages.",
